※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=-4 diag=none

※ The most negative number divided by minus one has no answer either: the
※ quotient is one past the largest the type can hold.  It is the only pair
※ that overflows, and the only one an unsigned type never meets.

let smallest: i8 = ⁻128i8
let minus_one: i8 = ⁻1i8

@[visible]
let kept: mut i8 = 0i8

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    kept ← smallest ÷ minus_one
    0u8
